Z||000004||The Fieromaster||07-10-2001||01:47 AM||||I want these rims sooo Hella bad!! They are Concept Neeper FLY rims.  Come in 17 18 and 20 inches AND in our bolt pattern!  Downside?  1,600 a set for RIMS ONLY!!  But DAMN they would look good on a Fiero.. HEY YOU IMAGE GUYS... think you could possibly please put those rims on my car so i can see what they would look like?<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Neeper_-_FLY_small.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>      "Raced That Wrecked Better"<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">     <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>AIM: Fieromaster<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||1
Z||000005||TRiAD||07-10-2001||03:59 PM||||Good wheel companies...hmm...<P>Well, it depends on useage. "Bad" wheel companies are far easier...<P>For cost-no-object wheels, Simmons (Aussie wheels), Fiske, Racing Hart, <B>OZ</B>, Volk, Kinesis...there are others...<P>For inexpensive lightweight wheels; you're basically limited to SSR and Kosei.<P>For "pimp" wheels (BIG heavy "show" wheels); Quantum Tek (QT), Niche and Neeper (same wheels, and buy ONLY from authorized dealers, WITH the warranty on the finish, I've seen the chrome strip off in weeks before! Usually good, though.), MKW, MHT, and more.<P>For "everyday" wheels; basically everything from Discount Tire, Tire Rack (although I've had better luck with Discount), and many of the "Sport Compact Car" dealers. Konig, Tenzo, BBS and more..<P><B>AVOID</B><BR>TSW, Savas (wheel dealer), Team Dynamics, MMR (Mantaray Motorsport Racing)/Landspeed (brothers, and dealers), and more...<P>Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Slammed Fiero||07-10-2001||04:41 PM||||Don't cheap on wheels. I got my Tr motorsports wheels through tirerack and there really good quality.<P>I have seen cheap import tuner wheels that leak because the casting is so porous.<P>I plan to get a set of HRE wheels for my car for street and keep the TR motorsports for track and autocross use in the next 2 years. (after motor swap)<P>We run Fikse's on our vette...simply amazing , but you pay for them. <P>JM ||||reg||1
